{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For a curse of Elohim is he who is hanged.</b> Now every separate essence that is distinct from matter is called Elohim, and of this kind is the essence of the rational soul in man, which is called צֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים (Genesis 1:27). On this basis the mistress of the ov said to Saul (1 Samuel 28:13): אֱלֹהִים רָאִיתִי עֹלִים — \"I saw Elohim rising.\" And since the indignity done to the dead after death is an indignity to the rational soul, which is a separate essence that endures after the death of the body, he said that it is a curse of Elohim — for leaving the hanged body unburied is an indignity to that eternal essence called Elohim." "<b>And you shall not defile.</b> [Do not] cause the spirit of impurity to dwell in the place of the unburied dead as it decomposes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The mistress of the ov is the woman at En-dor; Sforno's citation of 1 Samuel 28:13 uses the plural אֱלֹהִים in its sense of separate spiritual essences."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:58.763375752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}